# The 2026-09-15 ruling refuses a raised err at an operator at check, reading
# a call's arguments and not the names it is handed; bound to a name, a failure
# still reaches the comparison at runtime. Under the railway two failures
# merged here into one reason listing both, the 2026-08-05 reading; since
# 2026-09-16 the operator halts on the first, the left, and says so. The
# report is the interpreter's sentence, and native and the page say it too.
fn boom what
  err what

ea = boom "a"

eb = boom "b"

pub play = print "{ea < eb}"
